WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.570
. Joe Biden believes that Donald Trump should
not continue receiving intelligence briefings

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.380
and is going to stop them.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.980
Joe Biden was interviewed on CBS Evening News
on Friday.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.600
Norah O'Donnell asked him about this and Joe
Biden said he should stop getting the intelligence

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.710
briefings.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:24.439
You may know, you may not you may know that
former presidents receive intelligence briefings

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:27.300
even thereafter, even after they're out of
office.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.420
And it includes classified information.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.590
But we have a very I don't want to say very
unique.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:34.910
It's just unique.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.640
It's a unique situation in which Donald Trump
continuing to receive these briefings may

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.250
actually pose a national security risk.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:47.350
And Trump Trump couldn't even be trusted with
classified information as president.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:53.260
Of course, he can't be trusted with classified
information back as a private citizen.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:59.490
And this is the first time that a former president
is being cut out of briefings.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:06.530
And here is Joe Biden explaining why should
former President Trump still receive intelligence

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:07.530
briefings?

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.180
I think not.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.190
Why not?

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:17.780
Because of his erratic behavior unrelated
to the insurrection.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.210
I mean, you've called him an existential threat.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.460
You've called him dangerous.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.770
You've called him reckless.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.490
You have I believe it.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:32.810
What's your worst fear if he continues to
get these intelligence briefings?

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:37.610
I'd rather not speculate out loud, I just
think that there is no need for him to have

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.970
that intelligence briefing.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.479
What value is giving him an intelligence briefing?

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.780
What impact does he have at all other than
the fact he might slip and say something?

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.510
Joe Biden is absolutely correct.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:53.100
Donald Trump's intelligence briefings should
have been cut off on the first day that he

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.840
was out of office.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.530
Something nobody is saying but is relevant
is the question of is Trump even getting them?

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.080
If he is, is he listening?

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.260
If he's listening?

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.270
Does he remember or understand the content
of them?

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.619
And then what is he doing with that information
morally?

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:16.010
Donald Trump is exactly the type of person
who would figure out how to monetize or trade

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.540
access to that information if he came up with
a way to do it.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.760
I don't know that he's actually clever enough
to figure out a way to do it.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.120
But Trump is a sort of like who's the highest
bidder for what I know type of guy.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.660
Why even take a chance?

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.790
Democratic Congressman Adam Schiff has been
talking about this for a while.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.540
He said a couple of weeks ago, days before
Trump left office, a Trump shouldn't get these

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.540
briefings.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.319
And he makes another great point as to why
he leaves office.

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:44.480
He should be denied access to intelligence
briefings.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.819
Would you urge the Biden administration to
do that?

00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:54.090
Absolutely, there's no circumstance in which
this president should get another intelligence

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.180
briefing, not now, not in the future.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.130
I don't think he can be trusted with it now
and in the future.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.340
He certainly can't be trusted.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:06.239
Indeed, there were, I think, any number of
intelligence partners of ours around the world

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:12.190
who probably started withholding information
from us because they didn't trust the president

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:16.290
would safeguard that information to protect
the sources and methods.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.849
This is a really good point.

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:24.500
Aside from what Trump will do with the information,
we know that during Trump's presidency, many

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:29.700
of our allies were being more careful about
what they told the United States for fear

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.580
it would get to Trump and Trump would spill
the beans.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:37.260
If they know Trump still gets intelligence
briefings that might continue cutting Trump

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.959
off from the intelligence briefings.

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:45.330
Not only is the right decision from a national
security standpoint, it probably helps revive

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:50.569
some of our relationships, including as far
as intelligence sharing is concerned with

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:51.569
other countries.

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:56.760
That's something that is a big task for Joe
Biden, reestablishing some of those damaged

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.090
relationships.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.641
Joe Biden is right to do this.

00:03:59.641 --> 00:05:26.500
And the official announcement about it happening
should be coming any moment now.

